FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: minValueNode
Signature: struct node* minValueNode(struct node* node)
Description: /**
 * @brief Find the node with the minimum key in a binary search tree.
 *
 * Traverses the left subtree of the given node to locate the node with
 * the smallest key value. If the input node is NULL, returns NULL.
 *
 * @param node Root of the subtree to search. May be NULL.
 *
 * @return Pointer to the node with the minimum key, or NULL if node is NULL.
 */
Dependencies: None

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called minValueNode
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

struct node {
	int key;
	struct node *left, *right;
};

// Target function implementation
struct node* minValueNode(struct node* node)
{
	struct node* current = node;

	while (current && current->left != NULL)
		current = current->left;

	return current;
}

```

TARGET EXECUTION PATH:
Path 1: START | START --> STATEMENT | struct node* current = node; --> STATEMENT | (current && current->left != NULL) --> FOR_EXIT | loop exit --> RETURN | return current;

IMPORTANT: Choose inputs that satisfy this path's conditions.

